Code of Conduct
Our Pledge
We are committed to making participation in our project and community a welcoming, respectful, and positive experience for everyone, regardless of age, background, level of experience, education, nationality, personal identity, or any other characteristic.

We pledge to create an open and friendly environment where everyone can contribute, learn, and collaborate.

Our Standards
Examples of behavior that contributes to a positive environment include:

Being respectful and considerate toward others.
Using welcoming and inclusive language.
Respecting different viewpoints and experiences.
Accepting constructive criticism gracefully.
Giving and receiving feedback politely.
Helping beginners understand the project.
Focusing on what is best for the community.
Taking responsibility for mistakes and learning from them.
Examples of unacceptable behavior include:

Using insulting, offensive, or discriminatory language.
Harassment, threats, or personal attacks.
Publishing another person's private information without permission.
Trolling, deliberately disrupting discussions, or engaging in abusive behavior.
Any conduct that is inappropriate or harmful in a professional or educational setting.
Our Responsibilities
Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying and enforcing the standards of acceptable behavior. They may remove, edit, or reject comments, commits, code, issues, and other contributions that violate this Code of Conduct.

Project maintainers will communicate appropriate and fair corrective actions when necessary.

Scope
This Code of Conduct applies to all project spaces, including:

GitHub repositories and issue discussions.
Pull requests and code reviews.
Project-related communication channels.
Any situation in which an individual represents the project or its community.
Reporting Issues
If you experience or witness unacceptable behavior, please contact the project maintainer through the contact information provided in the repository.

All reports will be reviewed respectfully and handled as confidentially as reasonably possible.

Consequences
Behavior that violates this Code of Conduct may result in corrective action, including a warning, removal of inappropriate content, temporary restriction from project participation, or permanent exclusion from the project, depending on the severity of the incident.

Project maintainers will make reasonable efforts to handle reports fairly and consistently.

Attribution
This Code of Conduct is inspired by the Contributor Covenant, a widely used open-source community standard.

For more information, visit: https://www.contributor-covenant.org/

Conclusion
We encourage everyone to contribute positively, communicate respectfully, and help maintain a friendly and inclusive environment for learning and collaboration.

Thank you for helping make this project a welcoming place for everyone.
